      "message": "in idletimer_tg_target all we are doing is reset the timer whenever the packet matches with iptable rule . \n\nunsigned long now \u003d jiffies;\ninfo-\u003etimer-\u003eactive \u003d true;\n\n// We are resetting the timer when the timer.expires(specified timeout) \u003e now (current time)\nif (time_before(info-\u003etimer-\u003etimer.expires, now)) {\n\tschedule_work(\u0026info-\u003etimer-\u003ework);\n\tpr_debug(\"Starting timer %s (Expired, Jiffies): %lu, %lu\\n\",\n\t           info-\u003elabel, info-\u003etimer-\u003etimer.expires, now);\n}\n\nThe same logic , i,e resetting the timer with timer.expires is taken care in reset_timer function . \n\nPlease check line number 449 ,454 , 456 , 471 . We have removed this block in idletimer_tg_target_v1 as this seems to be duplicate code . \n\nTest cases with respect to timer reset logic are passing for both IDLETIMERs and ALARMTIMERS.",
